    {
      "id": "claim_435f2eab31da4881a62dddfa601c8219",
      "statement": "Migrations are applied automatically only for the local bundled Postgres: make up migrates before starting the backend when ENV=local, and make seed depends on migrate only locally. For managed/staging databases migration is deliberately a separate explicit step (make migrate ENV=staging) because the instance can be many migrations behind and needs a backup first.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L103-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51e19a578ba35c3ea1c3e714d1ca30b4f99650f0f8e769052b5f2513b62cdedb:"
