    {
      "id": "claim_b87a90477da7474aa49a19fb880d4140",
      "statement": "Router code takes PoolDep, a CallerPool: each connection is one transaction that first sets the Postgres role (anon or authenticated, anon when unauthenticated), request.jwt.claims and a statement_timeout (default db_statement_timeout_ms) with SET LOCAL in one round trip, so RLS and grants apply to the route and the connection returns to the pool as the owner. OwnerPoolDep is the plain shared owner pool, used by identity code and by staff/Import and other routes, and it bypasses RLS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/app/core/config.py#L144-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d4dffda7bbaad217f3b68e6821217089c534ddac147d0bc70e3bd5f312d1c211:"
